Chapter: LensForm
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 The explore page posts an urlencoded body: pairs split on ampersand, each
 pair on its first equals sign. A plus decodes to a space and a percent with
 two hex digits to the byte it names, mapped into CCE by from-unicode; a
 malformed escape stays a literal percent, and a byte outside CCE's tier-zero
 table is dropped.

 Memory posture (Rule 8): every loop below walks its input by index
 with an explicit stop, the accumulators are bounded by the body
 length, and a parsed form dies with the request that carried it.
 Nothing here retains, caches, or grows across calls.

Section: Hex Digits

  form-hex-val : Text -> Integer
  form-hex-val (c) =
    if c == "0" then 0
    else if c == "1" then 1
    else if c == "2" then 2
    else if c == "3" then 3
    else if c == "4" then 4
    else if c == "5" then 5
    else if c == "6" then 6
    else if c == "7" then 7
    else if c == "8" then 8
    else if c == "9" then 9
    else if (c == "a") | (c == "A") then 10
    else if (c == "b") | (c == "B") then 11
    else if (c == "c") | (c == "C") then 12
    else if (c == "d") | (c == "D") then 13
    else if (c == "e") | (c == "E") then 14
    else if (c == "f") | (c == "F") then 15
    else -1

Section: Decoding

 One pass over the encoded text. A plus becomes a space. A percent
 with two hex digits in range becomes the character whose ASCII code
 they spell, mapped into CCE by from-unicode; a code the table does
 not carry is dropped. A percent that is not followed by two hex
 digits passes through as itself, so a malformed escape is visible in
 the decoded value instead of swallowing the characters after it.

  form-decode : Text -> Text
  form-decode (t) = form-decode-loop t 0 (text-length t) ""

  form-decode-loop : Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  form-decode-loop (t) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else let ch = char-to-text (char-at t i)
    in if ch == "+" then form-decode-loop t (i + 1) len (acc & " ")
    else if ch /= "%" then form-decode-loop t (i + 1) len (acc & ch)
    else if i + 2 >= len then form-decode-loop t (i + 1) len (acc & ch)
    else let hi = form-hex-val (char-to-text (char-at t (i + 1)))
    in let lo = form-hex-val (char-to-text (char-at t (i + 2)))
    in if (hi < 0) | (lo < 0) then form-decode-loop t (i + 1) len (acc & ch)
    else let cce = from-unicode (hi * 16 + lo)
    in if cce < 0 then form-decode-loop t (i + 3) len acc
    else form-decode-loop t (i + 3) len (acc & char-to-text (code-to-char cce))

Section: The Fields

  LensFormFields = record {
    ff-dims : List Text,
    ff-meas : List Text,
    ff-limit : Integer
  }

  form-all-digits : Text, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  form-all-digits (t) (i) (len) =
    if i >= len then True
    else if is-digit (char-at t i) then form-all-digits t (i + 1) len
    else False

  form-int : Text -> Integer
  form-int (t) =
    if text-length t == 0 then 0
    else if form-all-digits t 0 (text-length t) then text-to-integer t
    else 0

  form-take : LensFormFields, Text, Text -> LensFormFields
  form-take (f) (key) (val) =
    if key == "dim" then
      (if text-length val == 0 then f
       else LensFormFields { ff-dims = list-push (f.ff-dims) val, ff-meas = f.ff-meas, ff-limit = f.ff-limit })
    else if key == "meas" then
      (if text-length val == 0 then f
       else LensFormFields { ff-dims = f.ff-dims, ff-meas = list-push (f.ff-meas) val, ff-limit = f.ff-limit })
    else if key == "limit" then LensFormFields { ff-dims = f.ff-dims, ff-meas = f.ff-meas, ff-limit = form-int val }
    else f

Section: Parsing

  form-eq-index : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  form-eq-index (t) (i) (len) =
    if i >= len then -1
    else if char-to-text (char-at t i) == "=" then i
    else form-eq-index t (i + 1) len

  form-pair : LensFormFields, Text -> LensFormFields
  form-pair (f) (part) =
    let eq = form-eq-index part 0 (text-length part)
    in if eq < 0 then form-take f (form-decode part) ""
    else form-take f (form-decode (substring part 0 eq)) (form-decode (substring part (eq + 1) (text-length part - eq - 1)))

  form-parse-loop : List Text, Integer, LensFormFields -> LensFormFields
  form-parse-loop (parts) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length parts then acc
    else form-parse-loop parts (i + 1) (form-pair acc (list-at parts i))

  lens-form-parse : Text -> LensFormFields
  lens-form-parse (body) =
    form-parse-loop (text-split body "&") 0 (LensFormFields { ff-dims = [], ff-meas = [], ff-limit = 0 })
